  "scientific_contract": {
    "hypothesis": "Direct hot-gas cooling/free-fall, cooling/sound-crossing, and cooling/cosmic clock organization contains held-out information about the weak-lensing-to-observed-gas mass discrepancy beyond the raw ACCEPT density, temperature, entropy, luminosity, gas-mass, cooling-time, redshift, and LC2 source-family variables.",
    "attempt_scope": "A small, contamination-safe independent cluster lane: direct ACCEPT cooling profiles at 20, 50, and 100 kpc paired only after a sample freeze with heterogeneous published LC2 weak-lensing M500 values.",
    "primary_response": "log10[(LC2 M500 in Msun)/(ACCEPT gas mass enclosed within 100 kpc in Msun)]",
    "strong_baseline": "fixed ridge model of every raw source variable used to construct the timescales, log10(1+Lbol) so published zero/missing luminosities remain target-blind, preregistered radial gradients/concentrations, and broad LC2 source-family nuisance controls",
    "interpretation_boundary": "LC2 M500 is a heterogeneous literature weak-lensing mass standardized under GR/cosmology/model assumptions, not direct shear, a direct CLASH observable gate, or evidence for modified gravity. ACCEPT gas mass within 100 kpc omits stars and outer gas; baryon-only free-fall is an intentionally incomplete diagnostic clock."
  },
